From: jorink <maxjorink@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vim keys: hjkl, g/G, Ctrl+U/D/B/F everywhere

Ported from KoffeinFlummi/htop-vim (last updated for htop 3.2.2) to 3.5.3,
with one translation point instead of per-panel cases: Panel_vimKey() maps
h/j/k/l to the arrows, g/G to Home/End and Ctrl+B/F to PgUp/PgDn, except
while the panel takes text (cursorOn: search, filter, renaming, number
entry). ScreenManager (main screen, setup, pickers) and InfoScreen (lsof,
env, strace) call it before any handler sees the key. Ctrl+U/D scroll half
a page. Keys that moved: kill k -> x, lsof l -> L, file locks x -> X, help
h -> F1 / ?. In type-to-jump lists, h j k l g G no longer jump; in setup's
Available Meters, `l` no longer adds to the left column (`L`, F5 still do).
---
